<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mashonaland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mashonaland is the region of northern and north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> inhabited mainly by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shona">Shona</a> people. Claimed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele</a> kingdom, it was occupied in 1890 by the Pioneer Column of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company">British South Africa Company</a>, which founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harare">Fort Salisbury</a>, later Harare. Its people rose against company rule in 1896–1897, and today it forms three provinces of Zimbabwe.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mashonaland.jpg" alt="Mashonaland" width="320" height="292" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mangwanani using Inkscape · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mashonaland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
